WEBVTT

00:00:59.355 --> 00:01:01.785
this pandemic, 
known technically as COVID-19,

00:01:01.809 --> 00:01:04.760
and informally as just the coronavirus,

00:01:04.784 --> 00:01:07.681
I find his thinking unbelievably helpful.

00:01:07.705 --> 00:01:10.054
And I'm excited to dive into it with you.

00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:12.483
A special callout to my friends on Twitter

00:01:12.507 --> 00:01:14.824
who offered up many
suggestions for questions.

00:01:14.848 --> 00:01:18.022
I know this topic
is on everyone's mind right now.

00:01:18.046 --> 00:01:19.998
And what I hope this episode does

00:01:20.022 --> 00:01:22.346
is give us all a more nuanced way

00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:26.085
of thinking about how this pandemic
has unfolded so far,

00:01:26.109 --> 00:01:27.847
what might be to come

00:01:27.871 --> 00:01:30.499
and what we all collectively
can do about it.